Protecting your wedding rental items usually means one thing: who pays if a rented chair, tent or tablecloth gets damaged. Malaga Event Gear does not rent any of those, and we do not publish a damage deposit or liability policy for our audio visual equipment either. What we can tell you, honestly, is how the [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) delivery only model and live on site technician protect the sound, lighting and microphones we do rent. For the full picture of what we cover for weddings, see our [wedding rentals](/blog/wedding-rentals/) overview.

## Brief Overview

---

Most guides answering "protecting your wedding rental items" default to furniture, tents and tableware, the trade MEG does not work in. The honest, AV specific version asks something different: how does a wedding's sound system, lighting rig and microphones survive a full day of guests, weather and a packed reception floor. The answer is not a damage waiver, it is professional installation, continuous on site monitoring, and a scope that stays inside what our crew actually controls.

## Key Highlights

---

-   Malaga Event Gear has no published damage deposit or liability policy for rental equipment. Ask us directly at the quote stage if that matters to your planning.
-   The [Wedding Pack's](/packages/wedding/) delivery only model means our own crew installs and calibrates every system, so no guest or venue staff ever handles raw AV gear.
-   A live technician stays on site through the reception, catching a loose cable or a stand out of place before it becomes damage.
-   Wind, rain and equipment placement outdoors get their own depth in our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide.
-   Furniture, tents, linens and tableware protection are outside our scope. See [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) for that full list.
-   Still weighing whether renting AV makes sense for your wedding at all? Our [pros and cons of wedding rentals](/blog/pros-and-cons-of-wedding-rentals/) page lays out the real advantages and real limits side by side.

<InlineCTA />

## What "Protecting Your Rental Items" Means When the Item Is AV Gear

Ask that question of a furniture or tent rental company and the answer is usually a damage waiver: a flat fee, sometimes a percentage of the order, that caps what a couple owes if something breaks. Malaga Event Gear does not operate that way for audio visual equipment, and we have no published deposit or liability clause to point you to. If a specific policy matters to your planning, ask us directly at the quote stage rather than assuming a figure from a furniture rental site applies here too.

Worth knowing before you ask any vendor, not just us: damage to rented audio visual equipment is not usually covered by a general event liability insurance policy. Those policies typically protect against injury or property damage a couple causes to a venue, not damage to gear a vendor owns. If equipment protection matters to your budget, raise it with whoever you book, MEG included.

## How the Wedding Pack Actually Protects the Equipment

What actually protects the gear on the day is not a policy, it is how the [Wedding Pack](/packages/wedding/) gets delivered. MEG operates delivery only, there is no self pickup option, so every PA system, light and microphone arrives on our own transport, gets installed and calibrated by our crew, and never passes through a guest's hands before the event starts.

That installation is followed by a live technician who stays for the whole event rather than a single drop off delivery. Through the ceremony, the speeches and the switch to dance volume, the technician watches the same gear: adjusting a stand that has drifted, moving a cable out of a walkway before someone trips on it, keeping a microphone away from a spilled drink. That continuous attention is the same mechanism our crew used on a two day production in Benahavis, where our on site technicians monitored sound and video continuously from setup through the closing session. See our [Bmotion Benahavis production](/blog/news-malaga-event-gear-delivers-flawless-audiovisual-production-for-bmotion-in-benahavis/) writeup for what that looked like in practice.

The Eco Pack, up to 50 guests, does not include that live technician: our crew delivers, installs and tests it, then it runs unattended. For a wedding with more moving parts, the Wedding Pack's on site technician is the meaningful difference for equipment protection, not just sound quality.

## What Weather Means for the Equipment Outdoors

Most Malaga weddings we set up for are outdoors, at a finca, villa or beach venue, where wind and ground surface change where a speaker stand or lighting rig can safely go. Our technician reads that on site rather than following a fixed indoor layout. For the full wind, curfew and power planning that goes with an outdoor setup, see our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide.

## What This Guide Does Not Cover

Chairs, tables, linens, tableware and tents are not part of what MEG rents or protects, and keeping those in good condition is a different vendor's responsibility. Our [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) guide lays out that full list and where our AV slice fits inside it.

