## Booking and Service Area

Our services focus on Malaga and extend to Granada for rentals over 400 euros. There is no fixed booking window, only availability, so reach out once your date and venue are confirmed, and tell us at that point if a specific equipment protection question matters to your planning. See our [booking timeline](/blog/timeline-for-booking-wedding-rentals/) guide for more on that.

## Conclusion

Protecting your wedding rental items, for the equipment MEG actually rents, comes down to who installs it and who watches it, not a deposit clause we do not publish. Professional delivery only installation and, on the Wedding Pack, a live technician through the whole event are the real answer for AV gear. [Contact us](/contact/) to check availability for your date, or to ask about a specific equipment question before you book.

## FAQs

### Who is responsible if a rented item is damaged at my wedding?

Malaga Event Gear does not publish a damage deposit or liability policy for our AV equipment. Ask us directly at the quote stage if that matters to you. For furniture, tents or tableware, responsibility sits with whichever vendor supplied the item, not MEG.

### Do wedding rental companies charge a damage deposit?

Many do, often a flat fee or a small percentage of the order. Practices vary by vendor and by item category. MEG does not publish a figure for AV equipment, so confirm directly with any vendor, including us.

### Is damage to rented AV equipment covered by wedding liability insurance?

Not usually. A general event liability policy typically covers injury or property damage a couple causes to a venue, not damage to equipment a vendor owns. It is a fair question to raise with any vendor you book, MEG included.

### How is the sound and lighting protected outdoors?

Through professional installation and a live technician who reads wind and ground conditions on site rather than a fixed layout. For the full outdoor picture, power, curfews and placement, see our [outdoor wedding rental considerations](/blog/outdoor-wedding-rental-considerations/) guide.

### Does the Wedding Pack cover furniture, tent or tableware protection?

No. MEG supplies sound, lighting, microphones and a technician only. Furniture, tents, linens and tableware come from a different vendor. Our [essential items for wedding rentals](/blog/essential-items-for-wedding-rentals/) guide covers that full list.

### What are the most common damages with wedding rentals, and who pays for them?

For the furniture, tents, linens and tableware other vendors supply, a damage waiver or deposit is the usual answer, though the practice and figure vary by company. For the AV equipment MEG actually rents, we do not publish a damage figure or policy: professional installation and, on the Wedding Pack, a live technician who reacts to shifting weather or a bumped stand are the real protection, not a deposit clause. Ask any vendor, including us, for their specific terms at the quote stage rather than assume one applies.
